# `twoarity/as_text.hero` as it stood until 2026-10-17: `value` lent
# read-only past `printf`'s `...`, which panel 217's R3(c) refuses (defect
# 2102), since C reads what it is handed there as whatever type it asks for.
# The refusal lands HERE, on this module's `value`, and never on `as_int.hero`'s
# `value: i64`, the same C name bound at another shape in another module:
# found by its name alone, it was told there, as declared `cstr lent`.

extern "stdio.h"
    function printf(format: cstr lent, value: cstr lent) -> i32  #~ ffi_writable_parameter

function say(format: str, value: str) -> i32
    return printf(format: format.cstr(), value: value.cstr())
